      "extract": "Throughout the paper, $\\mathcal C$ denotes a fusion category (FC) over the field $\\mathbb C$ of complex numbers (see [@EGNO15] for definitions). Its simple objects are denoted $c_i$'s with $i=1,\\dots,\\text{rank}(\\mathcal C)$. We denote its fusion ring by $K(\\mathcal C)$. A pivotal structure $a:id_{\\mathcal C}\\cong(-)^{**}$ defines left and right quantum (or categorical) traces $\\text{tr}^{L/R}(a):1\\to1$. A pivotal",
