      "extract": "A rank one pre-MFC has only one simple object $1$. There are two pre-MFCs depending on the sign of categorical dimension $D(\\mathcal B)=\\pm1$. Since $1\\le\\text{FPdim}(\\mathcal B_A)\\le\\text{FPdim}(\\mathcal B)=1$, the only possibility is $$\\text{FPdim}(\\mathcal B_A)=1.$$ Accordingly, the algebra has $$\\text{FPdim}_{\\mathcal B}(A)=\\frac{\\text{FPdim}(\\mathcal B)}{\\text{FPdim}(\\mathcal B_A)}=1.$$ Since the only simple",
